 Saldaña's performance has been particularly striking in Season 3, which pushed Joe into unfamiliar territory by making her the target of an elaborate kidnapping plot. After surviving torture and losing a toe, she returned home only to discover that her husband and daughters had left her. When she thought things couldn't get worse, the Lioness Season 3 finale revealed that Aaliyah Amrohi (Stephanie Nur), Cruz's love interest from Season 1, was behind it all.
 It's a jaw-dropping cliffhanger. As we wait to see whether Joe gets another mission, Zoe Saldaña will star in the Netflix movie Positano , a promising new heist thriller that pairs her with another Oscar winner. The movie is an exciting addition to her upcoming slate, although it raises questions about her future on Lioness .
 'Positano' Has All the Ingredients of a Record-Breaking Netflix Heist Thriller
 Close Paramount 
 © Apple TV+ / Courtesy Everett Collection 
 Toni Collette confronts JK Simmons in Clint Eastwood's Juror #2 Warner Bros. 
 According to Netflix's Tudum announcement, Positano follows a charming jewel thief (Matthew McConaughey) who gives up his comfortable life to help a mysterious woman (Saldaña) plan a high-stakes heist. However, the heist's payoff promises to be more than financial, suggesting that the two thieves might have competing motivations.
 Positano will be directed by Daniel Roher, who won an Academy Award for his documentary Navalny and recently made his feature film debut with Tuner . The supporting cast is also impressive, as it includes Toni Collette, Karren Karagulian, Salvatore Esposito, Michele Savoia, and Lorenzo de Moor.
 Collette is always a welcome addition to an ensemble. Karagulian is also interesting, as he is following his acclaimed performance in Anora . Esposito has starred in several crime stories, including Gomorrah and Den of Thieves 2: Pantera . No release date has been announced, but the movie already shows promise.
