 As exciting as Positano sounds, Saldaña's future as Joe in Lioness is the bigger question. There have been rumors about the actress potentially leaving the Taylor Sheridan thriller , but her latest comments don't establish that she is preparing to walk away. In fact, she told PEOPLE that starring in and executive producing the series already demands a huge commitment.
 "I'm number one on the call sheet. I am first one in, last one out. I don't know if we're able to go to a Season 4. I don't know where he would take it."
 Still, the Season 3 finale gives Sheridan a natural opportunity to change the show's leadership structure. Joe's family has left her, and her position within the CIA could become complicated now that she's a major target. This is where Laysla De Oliveira's Cruz becomes even more important. After starting as Joe's recruit in the Lioness Program , Cruz has become an experienced operative.
 In an interview with MovieWeb , De Oliveira discussed the possibility of Cruz moving into a higher position of authority. She said:
 "I think she's incredibly smart. Taylor [Sheridan] described her, and I agree with him completely, 'She's a wild cat with a heart of gold.' And so seeing how she approaches a higher position of authority with those dynamics is really interesting. It certainly seems like it's heading in that direction. I think she will be surprised when she finds herself there."
 Lioness Season 4 could explore that transition, with Cruz taking on more responsibility as Joe figures out whether she can continue leading the program. That doesn't necessarily mean replacing Saldaña as the lead, though. Joe and Cruz's relationship remains central to the show's identity, and Aaliyah's revenge plot gives them an unfinished story to resolve.
 'Lioness' Season 4 Renewal Is Delayed Due to Sheridan's Complicated Future
 Paramount+ 
 ​​Paramount+ hasn't renewed Lioness for Season 4 , but the third season's premiere attracted 7.1 million viewers in its first seven days, and it outperformed Season 2's debut. There is also a significant behind-the-scenes development. Writer Michael Idov revealed that he and his wife, Lily, joined as writers and supervising producers. They added that it was an honor to work with Saldaña, Nicole Kidman, and Morgan Freeman.
 The cast is optimistic, too. Jill Wagner recently told ScreenRant , "We're going to get a season 4. We will, we will." She even offered to pay $100 if Sheridan's finale didn't convince viewers that another season was coming. Meanwhile, my MovieWeb interview with Stephanie Nur offered an enticing glimpse into what could follow Aaliyah Amrohi's return .
 When discussing her character's feelings toward Cruz​​​​​​​ , Nur explained, "There's always a very thin line between love and hate." She added that anger and resentment often come from "a lot of love underneath there that has been hurt." When asked about the possibility of Season 4, she also said, "We don't know yet if we have one. But fingers crossed."
